---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="What Fieldnotes is, and how it's made.">
	<div class="shell">
		<header class="page-head">
			<span class="mono-label">About</span>
			<h1>A notebook,<br />kept in public.</h1>
		</header>

		<div class="measure" style="padding-bottom:2rem">
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					Fieldnotes is a personal publication about the craft of building software.
					It favors long essays over hot takes, revision over velocity, and the kind
					of writing you can return to a year later and still find useful.
				</p>
				<p>
					The premise is simple: the interesting parts of engineering happen in the
					margins — the naming decisions, the deleted code, the README nobody read.
					This site exists to write those margins down.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="colophon" style="border-top:1px solid var(--line)">
			<div>
				<h2>Colophon</h2>
				<p>Set in Fraunces and Inter, with JetBrains Mono for the apparatus. Built with Astro, deployed as static files. No trackers, no comments, no feed algorithm.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
				<p>Subscribe via <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>. Source code lives on <a href="https://github.com/wallus-src/dev">GitHub</a>. Correspondence welcome by reply-post — the old-fashioned way.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h2>Principles</h2>
				<p>Publish rarely. Revise often. Own the URL. Fast pages are a feature. Everything here is a draft that shipped.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Base>
